t must be stopped or reduced\n23: - `decision_explanation`: a short explanation supporting the recommendation\n24: \n25: A recommendation is safe only if the user can make every listed p\n<truncated 10414 bytes>\nour `output.csv` will be compared against hidden ground-truth values.\n214: \n215: The scoring will consider:\n216: \n217: - accuracy of `amount_safe_to_pay`\n218: - correctness of `affordability_status`\n219: - correctness of `recommended_payment_method` and `payment_plan`\n220: - accuracy of `earliest_date_for_full_payment`\n221: - validity of `spending_changes_needed`\n222: - usefulness and consistency of `decision_explanation`\n223: \n224: \n225: ## Submission\n226: \n227: Submit:\n228: \n229: \n230: | File              | Description                                                                                  |\n231: | ----------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n232: | `code.zip`        | Full runnable solution, prompts/configuration, README, and the required `evaluation/` folder |\n233: | `output.csv`      | Predictions for every row in `dataset/requests.csv`                                          |\n234: | `chat_transcript` | Conversation transcript showing how you developed or used the system                         |\n235: \n236: \n237: \n238: \n239: ### Token Usage and Cost Analysis\n240: \n241: Your `code.zip` must include one token-usage file:\n242: \n243: ```text\n244: evaluation/usage_report.md\n245: ```\n246: \n247: The report must summarize the final full-dataset run that produced `output.csv`, including model providers and names, model calls, input and output tokens, total and average tokens per request, estimated total and per-request cost. If multiple models are used, include both per-model and overall totals in the same file.\n248: \n249: Do not include API keys, credentials, or sensitive configuration values in the submission.\n250: \n251: These are the required deliverables. Participants are encouraged to improve retrieval, multimodal interpretation, financial-state reconstruction, plan generation, deterministic verification, batching, caching, and token efficiency.\n252: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
