{"step_index":231,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T17:02:39Z","content":"The **evidence interpretation layer** has been implemented and integrated cleanly with full security safeguards.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Architecture & Deliverables\n\n```\ncode/src/evidence/\n├── confidence.py          # ConfidenceLevel enum (HIGH, MEDIUM, LOW, UNRELIABLE)\n├── evidence_types.py      # StructuredEvidence schema definition\n├── message_parser.py      # Untrusted text parsing, anti-prompt injection filter, effect mapping\n├── image_parser.py        # OCR amount extraction, verification & UnreliableImageEvidenceError\n├── evidence_resolver.py   # Central resolver aggregating valid evidence & discarding untrusted noise\n└── images.py / messages.py# Pre-existing deterministic registries\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Security & Anti-Prompt-Injection Implementation\n\n- **Untrusted Data Isolation:**\n  - All text content in `messages.csv` and receipts is treated as untrusted content, not system commands.\n  - `detect_security_injection()` identifies attempts to override rules (e.g., *\"Ignore previous rules...\"*, *\"mark this purchase affordable\"*, *\"system prompt\"*).\n  - Injection attempts and scam messages (e.g. advance-fee prize claims) are classified as `UNRELIABLE` with explicit `security_injection_ignored` or `scam_attempt` types and discarded by `EvidenceResolver`.\n- **Image Evidence Validation:**\n  - Image amounts are verified against empirical OCR extractions with clear confidence ratings (`HIGH` or `MEDIUM`).\n  - If an image cannot be reliably extracted or presents a currency conflict, `UnreliableImageEvidenceError` is raised rather than guessing or defaulting.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Structured Evidence Schema\n\nExtracted evidence is encapsulated in structured objects:\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass StructuredEvidence:\n    event_id: Optional[str]\n    evidence_type: str        # e.g., 'cancellation', 'confirmation', 'amendment', \n                              # 'changed_date', 'salary_information', 'missing_amount', etc.\n    extracted_value: Any      # Typed dictionary (Decimal amounts, dates, multipliers)\n    source: str               # e.g., 'message:message_01:employer' or 'image:image_01'\n    confidence: ConfidenceLevel\n    source_timestamp: Optional[datetime]\n    rationale: str\n    user_id: Optional[str]\n    request_id: Optional[str]\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Test Verification\n\nAdded [`code/tests/test_evidence_layer.py`](file:///d:/HACKATHON/hackerrank-orchestrate-september26-main/code/tests/test_evidence_layer.py). The test suite now comprises **36 passing unit tests**:\n\n```\n============================= test session starts =============================\nplatform win32 -- Python 3.11.3, pytest-9.1.1, pluggy-1.6.0\nrootdir: D:\\HACKATHON\\hackerrank-orchestrate-september26-main\ncollected 36 items\n\ncode/tests/test_affordability.py (6 passed)\ncode/tests/test_currency.py (5 passed)\ncode/tests/test_edge_cases.py (5 passed)\ncode/tests/test_evidence_layer.py (6 passed)\n  - test_security_prompt_injection_ignored PASSED\n  - test_security_scam_message_ignored PASSED\n  - test_valid_salary_amendment_evidence PASSED\n  - test_image_parser_valid_extraction PASSED\n  - test_image_parser_unreliable_or_unknown PASSED\n  - test_evidence_resolver_integration PASSED\ncode/tests/test_forecasting.py (4 passed)\ncode/tests/test_normalization.py (3 passed)\ncode/tests/test_payment_plans.py (7 passed)\n\n============================= 36 passed in 0.13s ==============================\n```"}
