{"step_index":1063,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-13T08:02:35Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-13T13:32:35+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-13T13:32:35+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///d:/HACKATHON/hackerrank-orchestrate-september26-main/README.md`\nTotal Lines: 194\nTotal Bytes: 9961\nShowing lines 1 to 100\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # HackerRank Orchestrate\n2: \n3: Starter repository for the **HackerRank Orchestrate** 24-hour hackathon (September 2026).\n4: \n5: ## Buy or Wait?\n6: \n7: Build an AI-powered financial agent that decides whether a user can safely afford a requested expense.\n8: \n9: A user may ask: **\"Can I afford this laptop?\"**\n10: \n11: Answering well takes more than the current balance. The agent must account for recurring expenses, pending payments, essential spending, confirmed income, available payment options, and relevant details buried in messages and images.\n12: \n13: For every request, the agent decides whether the user should pay in full, pay partially, use installments, wait, or not proceed. The recommendation must be personalized: two users with the same balance can deserve different answers based on their commitments, priorities, payment preferences, and willingness to adjust flexible expenses.\n14: \n15: A recommendation is safe only if the user can complete the full payment plan, cover essential expenses, and stay above their preferred minimum balance throughout the forecast period.\n16: \n17: Read [`problem_statement.md`](./problem_statement.md) for the full task spec, input/output schema, allowed values, conflict-resolution rules, and submission format.\n18: \n19: ---\n20: \n21: ## Quick Start\n22: \n23: Clone the repository and move into the project directory:\n24: \n25: ```bash\n26: git clone https://github.com/interviewstreet/hackerrank-orchestrate-september26.git\n27: cd hackerrank-orchestrate-september26\n28: ```\n29: \n30: Build your solution in `code/main.py`, or use ano\n<truncated 1983 bytes>\nr request\n75:     ├── exchange_rates.csv            # Fixed, dated conversion rates\n76:     ├── messages.csv                  # Messages tied to users, requests, or events\n77:     ├── images.csv                    # Payroll letters, statements, bills, receipts\n78:     └── media/\n79:         └── images/\n80: ```\n81: \n82: Only `dataset/requests.csv` requires predictions. Everything else is context. Join user records with `user_id`, request records with `request_id`, supporting evidence with `related_event_id`, and exchange rates with the rate date and currency pair.\n83: \n84: Amounts are in the user's `home_currency` — the dataset uses INR, ZAR, IDR, USD, and EUR, and every conversion rate you need is in `exchange_rates.csv`. All dates are `YYYY-MM-DD`. Live exchange rates, market data, and banking access are not required.\n85: \n86: ---\n87: \n88: ## What You Need to Build\n89: \n90: For every row in `dataset/requests.csv`, produce one row in `output.csv` with:\n91: \n92: | Column | Meaning |\n93: |---|---|\n94: | `request_id` | The request being answered |\n95: | `amount_safe_to_pay` | Largest amount safe to pay on `request_date` before optional spending changes, after protecting essentials and the minimum balance |\n96: | `affordability_status` | `affordable_now`, `affordable_with_plan`, `affordable_later`, or `not_affordable` |\n97: | `recommended_payment_method` | `full_payment`, `partial_payment`, `installments`, `wait`, or `not_recommended` |\n98: | `payment_plan` | Chronological `<YYYY-MM-DD>:<amount>` entries joined by `\\|`, or `none` |\n99: | `earliest_date_for_full_payment` | Earliest date the full amount is forecast safe as one payment; empty if never within the forecast |\n100: | `spending_changes_needed` | Up to three `stop:<event_id>` / `reduce_to:<event_id>:<amount>` changes joined by `\\|`, or `none` |\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
