{"step_index":1690,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-13T09:09:12Z","content":"The recurring cash-flow projection engine has been rebuilt and audited against all specification requirements.\n\n---\n\n### Key Architectural Improvements\n\n1. **Canonical `RecurringStream` Model** ([`src/models/recurring_stream.py`](file:///d:/HACKATHON/hackerrank-orchestrate-september26-main/src/models/recurring_stream.py)):\n   - Represents each recurring series with explicit fields:\n     - `stream_id`, `user_id`, `category`, `event_type`, `direction`, `currency`\n     - `cadence` (`weekly`, `biweekly`, `monthly`, `irregular`)\n     - `period_days`, `amount_rule`, `base_amount`\n     - `historical_evidence`: list of settled antecedent transactions\n     - `scheduled_overrides`: explicit future scheduled occurrences\n     - `cancellation_date`: explicit termination date\n     - `projected_occurrences`: chronologically projected events\n\n2. **Multi-Cadence Regularity Detection** ([`determine_stream_cadence`](file:///d:/HACKATHON/hackerrank-orchestrate-september26-main/src/normalization/events.py#L34-L70)):\n   - Replaced simple average day difference with variance and spread checks:\n     - **Weekly**: intervals tightly bounded around 7 days (6–8 days).\n     - **Biweekly**: intervals tightly bounded around 14 days (12–16 days).\n     - **Monthly**: validates calendar day-of-the-month consistency ($\\le 3$ days variation) or strictly bounded monthly intervals (26–33 days).\n     - **Variance Isolation**: prevents irregular series (e.g. intervals of 11, 34, 43 days with an average of 29.3 days) from erroneously being classified as regular monthly streams.\n\n3. **Scheduled Overrides & Non-Suppressive Forward Filling** ([`project_recurring_events`](file:///d:/HACKATHON/hackerrank-orchestrate-september26-main/src/normalization/events.py#L140-L210)):\n   - **No Blind Suppression**: Previously, having a single scheduled event in a category suppressed projection for that category entirely. Now, existing scheduled events act as authoritative anchors for their scheduled dates.\n   - **Collision Defense**: Projection candidates within `period // 2` days of an authoritative scheduled event are omitted to prevent duplication.\n   - **Forward Continuation**: The stream projects forward past any scheduled events up to the end of the 90-day simulation horizon.\n\n4. **Preservation of Amendments & Cancellations**:\n   - Explicit salary increases, temporary salary adjustments, contract terminations (`employment_ended`), and 12% rent adjustments are applied cleanly over the full timeline (historical + scheduled overrides + projected occurrences).\n\n---\n\n### Adversarial Verification\n\nAdded 8 test scenarios in [`tests/test_recurring_stream_adversarial.py`](file:///d:/HACKATHON/hackerrank-orchestrate-september26-main/tests/test_recurring_stream_adversarial.py):\n- `test_adv_cadence_determination`: verifies weekly, biweekly, and monthly cadence identification.\n- `test_adv_historical_plus_one_scheduled_future`: confirms scheduled date is authoritative while subsequent months are correctly projected.\n- `test_adv_multiple_scheduled_overrides`: verifies multiple future scheduled events without duplicates.\n- `test_adv_salary_increase_amendment`: confirms amended salary rules apply across projected occurrences.\n- `test_adv_salary_decrease_temporary`: confirms temporary reduction impacts only the immediate cycle.\n- `test_adv_cancelled_salary`: confirms termination marks all subsequent occurrences as cancelled.\n- `test_adv_rent_increase_12pct`: confirms 1.12x lease escalation applies to recurring projections.\n- `test_adv_missing_month_stream` & `test_adv_irregular_dates`: validates robustness against missing intervals and non-regular date noise.\n\n---\n\n### Test & Evaluation Results\n\n- **Unit & Adversarial Tests**: `86 passed in 0.47s` (`pytest -q`).\n- **Full 250-Request Simulation**: Completed in **1.803s** (5